  "notes": [
    "Modelled as one 26 m shaft with flights and landings added as walk geometry, not as stacked chambers.",
    "The ringing floor and belfry gallery are annular. The client places an actor on the first surface a downward ray meets, so a full-footprint deck would ground every placement in the tower on the topmost floor. A player can still WALK the stair normally - only placement is single-layer - but no spawn or portal may sit beneath a deck."
  ],
